- Python-style project from the PyPI website
- The main essence of the PepeunitClient project
- The main entity of the PepeunitClient project, which users will interact with; all other entities are auxiliary and, if available to users, only through the PepeunitClient class object
- The project can be downloaded via pypi in 4 variations: without additional packages, rest, mqtt, all
- Type code as often as possible, but don't overdo it.
- Do not expand gitignore and do not delete files from the project root specified in it.
- Remove all functions, methods, attributes, and classes that are not used in the code base.
- Do not create redundant implementations, especially methods that will not be used anywhere later on.
- Comments are only allowed for class methods; they are not allowed elsewhere.
- Comments should be concise, describing what the method does without going into implementation details.
- Comments can only be in English.
- Project without tests, we will do the tests later
- Project without examples of work; we will do them later.
- Don't touch the readme.md, we'll write it at the very end, even after the tests and examples.
- context/tz.md contains tasks that PepeunitClient must solve.
- context/old_client.py - a test client that previously used the backend, containing basic REST requests and examples of almost all interactions via MQTT.